{
    "background_story": "Fernando was a skilled administrator and financial expert in ancient Rome. Born into a noble family, he was educated in law, politics, and economics. Fernando's exceptional abilities caught the attention of the Roman Senate, which appointed him as a quaestor, responsible for managing the empire's finances. He served with integrity and diligence, ensuring the efficient allocation of resources and uncovering corruption within the system. Fernando's tenure as quaestor was marked by significant reforms, including the establishment of a standardized accounting system and the reduction of unnecessary expenses. His dedication to public service earned him the respect of his peers and the gratitude of the Roman people. Fernando's legacy as a quaestor continued to inspire future generations of Roman leaders.",
